\title{tobit.mean: Calculate Descriptive Statistics of Censored Vectors}
\description{
Calculate descriptive statistics of left- and right-censored numeric vectors: the arithmetic mean, geometric mean, standard deviation, and percent coefficient of variation. Censoring is accounted for by maximum likelihood estimation with the Tobit model (Tobin (1958) \doi{10.2307/1907382}), using the convex reparameterization of the likelihood described by Olsen (1978) \doi{10.2307/1911445}, rather than by ignoring or substituting censored values.
}
